### Settings implementation traceability

Completion: 2026-10-06. Second review and independent stage-completion audit passed. Subagent validation: 120 focused cases passed (0 failed/skipped); Release build passed (0 errors, 6 existing warnings); diff checks passed. An executed regression demonstrated matrix overflow from finite authored values before the fix and passed after composed-matrix validation. Commands used VINTAGE_STORY=G:/Vintagestory: `dotnet build VanillaExpanded/VanillaExpanded.csproj -c Release --no-restore --verbosity minimal` and `dotnet test VanillaExpanded.Tests/VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj -c ToolHeadValidation --filter FullyQualifiedName~ToolHeadPresentationResolverTests --no-restore --verbosity minimal`. Rendering integration and visual acceptance remain outstanding.

- Settings resolution/defaults -> proposal Asset settings / Schema and transform convention -> [ToolHeadPresentationResolver](../../VanillaExpanded/src/ItemRendering/ToolHeadPresentationResolver.cs) reads only resolved collectible attributes, initializes `ModelTransform.ItemDefaultGui()`, and populates a seeded `ModelTransformNoDefaults` through engine `JsonUtil.PopulateObject` typed deserialization; the engine determines accepted fields and numeric conversions. [ToolHeadPresentationProperties](../../VanillaExpanded/src/ItemRendering/ToolHeadPresentationProperties.cs) owns the values and supplies independent draw copies.

Typed-deserialization refactor validation: 2026-10-06. The same commands passed 121 focused tests and the Release build (0 errors, 6 existing warnings). The added authored-sentinel regression reproduced unwanted default substitution before the input-type correction and passed afterward. Diff checks passed.
- Validation/fallback -> the same schema contract and proposal Coverage and fallback -> [ToolHeadPresentationResolution](../../VanillaExpanded/src/ItemRendering/ToolHeadPresentationResolution.cs) distinguishes missing, invalid, and valid configuration; typed deserialization failures, finite-value and positive-scale checks, and composed model-matrix finiteness checks prevent unusable configuration from returning usable properties.
- Bounded diagnostics -> proposal Coverage and fallback -> the client-thread resolver uses weak collectible identity and reports once per collectible for its lifetime, marking before invoking the diagnostic sink to prevent reentrant repeats. Current attributes are read again on resolution, so corrected configuration is not permanently cached as invalid.
- Focused verification -> proposal Validation and Phase 2 checks -> unit checks are run through a subagent; rendering integration and visual evidence belong to later tasks.

## Phase 3: Apply dedicated transforms to radial-menu draws

Depends on Phases 1–2. Outcome: supported configured tools render through a dedicated method using engine preparation and mesh submission, with independent presentation and no item-renderer patch.

Reopened on 2026-10-06 after approval to replace the hook design. Replacement drawing, cleanup, and integration completed on 2026-10-06 after fresh validation, second review, and independent stage-completion audit.

- [x] Supply wedge icon position, size, direction, and hover context to the focused item-rendering component without forcing unrelated artwork to opt in.
- [x] Resolve the proposal's required renderer decisions before dependent implementation.
  - [x] Document shader/state entry, applicable callback-prepared state, nested-draw behavior, and exception-safe exit/reset ownership.
  - [x] Select and document post-preparation behavior for changed stack, projection, renderer registration, or rendering support. Preserve the explicitly revised cancellation contract; never repeat preparation through an ordinary GUI retry.
- [x] Implement the dedicated prepared-item draw through public engine APIs.
  - [x] Select missing/invalid settings, known custom delegates, unsupported projections, and unavailable support through ordinary engine rendering before preparation, including the existing category offset.
  - [x] Call `GetItemStackRenderInfo(slot, Gui, dt)` once, preserving engine model selection, overlays, slot callbacks, and collectible callbacks. Match the current `dt = 0` convention.
  - [x] Check for a drawable prepared mesh and issue `InGuiIdle` once in the engine's documented order. Supersede inventory-transform changes with the authored matrix while preserving the lifecycle notification's other behavior.
  - [x] Recheck support and selected stack after callbacks/lifecycle notification, then follow the documented post-preparation policy without a second preparation or draw retry.
  - [x] Apply the agreed model rotation, scale, translation, and pivot, then optional wedge-relative screen rotation in the documented order.
  - [x] Apply menu size and hover consistently without double scaling or fixed screen placement.
  - [x] Validate the final presentation matrix after applying menu size, placement, and wedge rotation.
  - [x] Connect the existing matrix builder to the dedicated draw; omit the category head-centering offset for supported configured draws and retain it for ordinary fallback.
  - [x] Obtain the engine GUI shader; submit model, current projection, and current-model-view-composed matrices without applying inventory GUI presentation.
  - [x] Apply ordinary GUI shader settings for normal shading, color, alpha test, temperature/glow, damage, and overlays. Use public atlas-position lookup for overlay UV origin and preserve applicable GUI culling, blending, and depth behavior.
  - [x] Submit the borrowed prepared mesh with `RenderMultiTextureMesh(info.ModelRef, "tex2d", 0)`; do not add mesh uploads, retained geometry, or disposal of borrowed resources.
  - [x] Implement the agreed shader/state contract with `try/finally`, local owned matrices, and safe nested/failing draws. The renderer itself must not mutate collectible GUI transforms; item-owned lifecycle side effects remain allowed.
- [x] Retain existing icon capture, halo, hover, and wedge-stencil processing; allow intentional handle cropping.
- [x] Replace `QuickToolItemIcon`'s scoped request with direct routing to the dedicated renderer; preserve unrelated artwork and ordinary inventory behavior.
- [x] Remove `ToolHeadPresentationHook`, `ToolHeadPresentationScope`, patch installation/disposal and availability state, and hook-specific tests. Retain registry-access metadata caching where needed and keep the client composition root thin.
- [x] Through a subagent, validate one preparation and one applicable `InGuiIdle`, callback-selected mesh/settings, configured-transform independence from differing inventory GUI settings, preserved ordinary inventory, and every before/after-preparation fallback branch.
- [x] Through a subagent, validate shader settings and state restoration after nested calls and failures, plus absence of glow/overlay/damage/model state leaking to later icons or labels.
- [x] Through a subagent, rerun retained transform-composition coverage for wedge directions, authored pivots, menu sizes, GUI scales, and hover values with the dedicated integration.
- [x] Through a subagent, run the affected checks and Release build; review the complete revised contract twice and perform the independent stage-completion audit before marking replacement work complete.

Completion criteria:

- [x] Configured supported draws use public preparation/submission and the dedicated transform without inventory GUI transforms, category offsets, or item-renderer patching.
- [x] Both required renderer decisions are recorded and executed tests prove their single-preparation and state-cleanup contracts.
- [x] Ordinary inventory and unrelated menu artwork retain their behavior; all fallback conditions, GUI effects, and nested/failing cleanup have fresh focused evidence.
- [x] Superseded patch/scope code and tests are removed, while reusable settings/matrix/context coverage remains.
- [x] Clipping remains intentional rather than triggering automatic shrinking or fitting. Full GPU appearance remains separate user-run acceptance work in Phase 5.

### Historical hook implementation traceability

