### Final validation and acceptance traceability

Validation: 2026-10-06. Through a subagent, a fresh Release rebuild passed with 0 errors and 6 existing warnings; 354 affected tests passed with 0 failed/skipped, including the standalone actual OpenGL state-restoration fixture. Commands used `VINTAGE_STORY=G:/Vintagestory` and `G:/Vintagestory/Lib` on PATH: `dotnet build VanillaExpanded/VanillaExpanded.csproj -c Release --no-restore --target:Rebuild --verbosity minimal` and `dotnet test VanillaExpanded.Tests/VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj -c ToolHeadPhase5Validation --filter "FullyQualifiedName~ItemRendering|FullyQualifiedName~RadialMenu|FullyQualifiedName~QuickTool" --no-restore --verbosity minimal`. Existing Cake JSON validation passed via `dotnet run --project CakeBuild.csproj --no-restore -- --target=ValidateJson` from `CakeBuild`. Local inspection confirmed all 23 separate patch files contain one expected add operation each, matching 23 unique installed item targets. The removed installation-dependent asset-patching test and its dependency remain absent; prior executed engine patch-resolution results remain the historical evidence recorded above.

User-reported visual acceptance: 2026-10-06. Asked for results after loading the latest mod build across representative heads (including stone/metal and ruined variants), menu sizes, GUI scales, wedge positions, and resting/partial/full hover, covering readability, orientation, intentional handle cropping, halo appearance, stable placement, and glow/overlay/damage effects. The user replied: "its fine". This is acceptance of the requested visual scope, not an agent observation or a measurement report. No issue or tuning request was reported, so no asset adjustment or repeat visual check was required. No game was launched by the agent.

- Build and focused checks -> proposal Validation / Rendering behavior -> independent presentation, single preparation/lifecycle, fallback/cancellation, GUI effects, borrowed ownership and exceptional/nested cleanup -> fresh affected tests, actual GL restoration fixture, Release rebuild and existing JSON validation above.
